# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. A CRLF entrypoint.sh fails inside
# the container with the notoriously unhelpful:
#     exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# — the "missing file" is actually the \r glued onto the interpreter path.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher needs CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
# dataset/metrics.db is committed, and this machine has core.autocrlf=true.
# Git would almost certainly infer "binary" from the NUL at byte 15 of the
# "SQLite format 3\0" header and leave it alone — but that is a heuristic,
# and the failure mode is a database silently corrupted by \n -> \r\n on
# checkout. State it instead. `binary` also means -diff, so log and status
# stop trying to render an 8 MB blob as text.
*.db binary
dataset/metrics.db filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
